OrionLayer open fix 109 — the diplomacy system picker on the wire
=================================================================

Work order 322 part E ("the diplomacy system picker", from 321's part B).
orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open fix
108; commit 90656654. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In src/game/dip_scrn.cpp,
src/game/dip_scrn.h and src/ext/ext_api.cpp under ORION2RE_EXT.

DIP_SCRN::Diplomacy_System_Display (dip_scrn.cpp:701; the lines are the
branch's at d1efc870, just before this fix moved them), "choose a system to
offer / demand", opened from the audience's Offer Gift > System
(dip_scrn_main.cpp:390), Demand > Surrender System (dip_scrn.cpp:1555), the
better offer asked of any human target (:1195), and in a network game the
chat's Demand and Offer Gift (`Get_Net_Diplomacy_Choices`, :1966, :1971),
sets screen 6 (:710), which open fix
46's 57 / 58 override masks, and put nothing on the wire but its fields.
After its fields (:740) a TurnPopupGuard reports id 85 and TPOP kind 25
(the kind = id - 60 pairing of 20/80, 22/82, 23/83, 24/84; both free):
args [0] the giver, [1] the receiver, [2] display_mode (0 offer, 1
demand), [3] the CANCEL field (:740), [4] current_ambassador, [5]
ambassador_option; title choose_a_system_buffer ("Choose A System:",
JIMTEXT2 0x02), text diplomacy_message (the statement the room prints,
JIMTEXT2 0x37 / 0x3F decoded at :728-729). The tail, written on every
snapshot: five strings (int16 length + raw bytes) — CANCEL's words
(system_cancel_buffer), the star line's and the population line's
templates (JIMTEXT2 0x3A and 0x38, read once at the picker's start into
two static buffers, undecoded: the game's own buffers hold them decoded
for the last star hovered), " (HOMEWORLD)" and "(Unsurrenderable)";
int16 n (NUM_STARS), n x int16 star i's hidden field
(diplomacy_system_fields[i + 1], :734-738); int16 m, then for each star
Diplomacy_System_Scan answers with the giver: int16 star, int16
May_Surrender_Star (0 / 1), int16 the capitol's planet (-1 none), int16
Get_System_Population, int16 k, k x (int16 planet, string "size,
climate" as Draw_Diplomacy_System_Text prints it, :2364). Ended right
after the loop, before the fields are released. It changes no game
state; the two template reads pump Mox_Update as the original's own reads
do (the engine's comment says "Read only", meaning that).

Observed, not changed: the picker writes diplomacy_system_fields[NUM_STARS]
(MAX_STARS entries), one past the array in a galaxy of MAX_STARS stars; the
writer does not read that slot.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (Data's decision of 20 October 2026); built
and compiled (`linux-debug`, ORION2RE_EXT on; dip_scrn.cpp also without
it; a misspelt member refused by the compiler on the scratch clone).

